  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Health and Protection Assistance for Individuals in Libya Affected by the Conflict in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Heavy clashes between the Rapid Support Forces and the Sudanese Armed Forces that erupted on 15 April 2023 across Sudan has resulted in the displacement of more than 6 million people, with more than 2 million people having crossed to Sudan&#x2019;s neighbouring countries to flee the conflict. Through this rapid response allocation from the Central Emergency Response Fund, this project is contributing towards the alleviation of suffering and improvement of living conditions for Sudanese and host populations in various cities in the east of the country. Specifically, the International Organization for Migration is providing multisectoral lifesaving humanitarian assistance, focusing on protection services and health assistance, for Sudanese in Libya.</narrative>
  </description>
